# ==== D238 (gravity, 2026-09-24): the seams_init determinism lint back to green ====
# The Gravity crates (and a few shared ones) grew 148 unledgered sites between the permit-s1 train and the v4 switch; the
# lint was red on trunk and CT_SKIPped in the gate (D238, classified by M0-GATE: REAL / MECHANICAL / ALLOW). REAL sites were
# routed through the sanctioned surfaces (pg_strong_random, the fd layer, pg_clock, the waiter, the spawn door); MECHANICAL
# sites swapped their std::sync imports to pgsync. The rows below are the ALLOW class: each names its site and why it stays
# raw. Ratchet law from here: budgets only shrink.
env	crates/gravity/hosts/src/dict/text_hosts.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(d238): PGRUST_GRAVITY_FP_SEED, the 32-hex pin of the fingerprint seed (read once inside the seed draw; also the natural DST pin of the Fp128 keys); P2 knobs registry
once	crates/gravity/hosts/src/dict/text_hosts.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(d238): P3 row-19 boot-hoisted once-cell: the fingerprint SEED (pgsync::OnceLock) is drawn by the postmaster at boot (launch_backend gravity_prewarm_register -> fp_seed) before any backend exists, so no token holder races the init; its entropy (pg_strong_random) and seed file (fd layer) are sanctioned surfaces
spawn	crates/gravity/backend/src/cache.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(d238): row 16 CONVERTED: the GravityCodeCache parent-context helper thread (first code-cache miss, once per process) spawns through the pgsync::thread child-registering wrapper (scanner sees the textual thread::Builder, not the pgsync routing); it only builds a MemoryContext off every thread root forest and exits
join	crates/gravity/backend/src/cache.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(d238): P3 row-14 join-bounded-after-wake: made.join() on that helper, a pgsync::thread JoinHandle (a scheduled Join block_on under pgrust_sim); the child needs no run token and no lock to exit (it touches neither PARENT nor the cache)
once	crates/gravity/backend/src/cache.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(d238): P3 row-19 GUC-read once-cache: BUDGET (pgsync::OnceLock) reads pgrust.gravity_code_cache_mb through guc_seams once, else the cost home's RAM share (code_cache_bytes over the driver's machine profile); the closure crosses no choke point
time	crates/gravity/backend/src/cache.rs	6	DST-REVIEW(d238): observability only: Instant t0 -> Outcome.ns (the hit latency or the miss compile + insert), reported by the IR-probe and code-cache counters; no admission, eviction or plan decision reads it
time	crates/gravity/backend/src/wasm.rs	4	DST-REVIEW(wasmjit stage 2): observability only, the same class as cache.rs's row: the Instant import and compiled_all's t0 -> Outcome.ns (hit latency or the miss emit + install), reported by the code-cache counters; no install, eviction, fallback or plan decision reads it; the file is the wasm32 server's backend (cfg target_family = "wasm"), never built natively or under pgrust_sim
blocking	crates/gravity/backend/src/cache.rs	2	DST-REVIEW(contract-runtime C03 / DR-21): the code cache's in-flight wait (Flight::wait / land: a pgsync Mutex + Condvar per key): a miss whose key another thread compiles waits for that one compile, holding no lock; land wakes every waiter on every exit of the compile (an unwind's included), and a failed compile leaves no marker, so the wait is bounded by one compile
blocking	crates/gravity/backend/src/promote.rs	3	DST-REVIEW(contract-runtime C03 / DR-21): tier 0's compile pool: its queue (a pgsync Mutex) and two pgsync Condvars (WAKE: an idle pool thread waits for a job; IDLE: quiesce / stop wait for the queue to empty or the threads to end); no backend waits on the pool, a backend only waits on one key's compile (cache.rs)
blocking	crates/gravity/backend/src/lib.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(rxcursor D3811): fault injection only: pool_compiled_all's hold (pgsync::thread::sleep of PGRUST_GRAVITY_TIER0_HOLD_MS, an env var read once at server start, capped at the cost home's TIER0_HOLD_MAX_MS 60 s, unset = 0 = no sleep) runs on a compile pool thread inside its key's claim, so a promotion of the same module waits on it as on a long compile (the D3811 witness); no backend sleeps, no session can set it, and with the env unset the line never runs
spawn	crates/gravity/backend/src/promote.rs	1	DST-REVIEW(contract-runtime C03 / DR-21): tier 0's compile pool threads (COMPILE_POOL_THREADS, the cost home's: 1), spawned lazily at the first tier-0 miss through the pgsync::thread child-registering wrapper (scanner sees the textual thread::Builder), process-lifetime like the runtime pool's; promote::stop drops the queue and ends them; PGRUST_GRAVITY_TIER0_ASYNC=off spawns none
fs	crates/gravity/backend/src/dump.rs	7	DST-REVIEW(V4R-59): observability only: pgrust.gravity_dump_dir (superuser-only, empty = off) writes each compiled program's .ir / .<arch>.bin / .meta to that directory on a code-cache miss (create_dir_all + 3 writes + the BUILD stamp read); no plan, admission, result or cache decision reads it; off under pgrust_sim (never set) + DST-REVIEW(v5-L1 identity dump): +3 = gravity_backend::dump::write_prog (the identity gate's per-install record prog/<seq>.prog under pgrust.gravity_dump_dir, superuser-only, empty = off) and its load-bias read of /proc/self/exe + /proc/self/maps; observability only, cold, the same class as the V4R-59 rows
