# ==== V4R-145 (gravity R1b, 2026-09-25): the hosts reuse pool's idle release ====
# ==== pgrc delta-v2 (2026-09-26): the sites the pgrc branch added, back to trunk's zero violations ====
# The pgrc delta-v2 steps (F1/F2 front, K1 compaction, WR spool, C1 colcache, the vfs link commit) took the lint
# from trunk f12d90d24a6's 0 violations to 18 (16 unledgered files, 2 budget overruns). Routed, no row: compaction's
# pause / flush-cap / part-age clocks and the maintenance workers' sweep, linger, drain-wait, age and budget clocks
# onto pg_clock; compaction's part stat and dir scan and the catalog's deferred unlink onto vfs; the compaction pause
# sleep onto waiter::sleep; six std::sync Mutex / OnceLock statics onto pgsync. The rows below stay raw (the two
# budget bumps are on the vfs posix.rs and pgrc_am catalog.rs rows above). Ratchet law from here: budgets only shrink.
